# Committing it would make a derived artifact look like a source of truth.
.xp-gate/debt-breakdown.json

# Full-audit scratch (gitleaks history dumps, semgrep JSON, per-chunk principle
# scan output). Regenerated by every audit run and ~1.2MB of machine-specific
# findings, so it is output, never source. The rest of .xp-gate/ is ignored
# file-by-file above; this directory was the gap that kept reappearing as an
# untracked entry in `git status`.
.xp-gate/full-audit/

# Verification-time scratch (walkthrough drivers, adversarial probes, review
# round dumps) lives in one directory. Filename-prefix rules were tried first
# and rejected: `.cw-*` also swallows a legitimately committed file that happens
# to start with that prefix, and the other two prefixes matched nothing.
.agent-tmp/

